  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "Route path -> component is not claimed: the route table is the object-literal argument of createRouter, and omega-javascript/omega-typescript emit a fact for an object key only when its value is a function, so neither the path string nor the component identifier reaches the overlay.",
      "provide()/inject() keys are not claimed: the key is a string-literal first argument and call.function carries the callee name and nothing else, so a ContextKey entity would have nothing to be named by.",
      "The event names declared by defineEmits(['a','b']) are not claimed for the same reason. vue.macro.declares states that the component declares emits, and vue.template.event-listener states which events a parent listens for.",
      "Tag -> file resolution is by file stem, not by import: vue.template.renders.file joins the tag name to the data.file whose path.stem matches, so <UserCard/> reaches components/UserCard.vue, but a kebab-case tag (<user-card/>) does not, because no clause or key template can case-fold; those tags keep only the name-hub edge from vue.template.renders. data.vue_element spans only the tag name, so a prop or a listener written on the same tag still cannot be span-joined to it.",
      "A dynamic <component :is=\"x\"> target, an auto-imported component and a globally registered component are build-tool or runtime facts and are not claimed.",
      "TS/JS script semantics inside an SFC arrive through the omega-vue injection, which resolves lang=js/ts/mjs/cjs/jsx/tsx to the javascript or typescript Pack; there is no TSX Pack path, so a <script lang=\"tsx\"> block is analysed as TypeScript."
    ]
  },
